<section class="panel" id="analytics-settings"><p class="eyebrow">OWNER CONTROLS</p><h2>Collection &amp; retention</h2><form method="post" class="form-stack analytics-settings-form"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="settings"><label class="checkbox-label"><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" value="1" <?=$options['enabled']?'checked':''?>><span>Collect public visitor analytics</span></label><label class="checkbox-label"><input type="checkbox" name="geo_enabled" value="1" <?=$options['geo_enabled']?'checked':''?>><span>Estimate approximate location using local data</span></label><label class="checkbox-label"><input type="checkbox" name="bot_tracking_enabled" value="1" <?=$options['bot_tracking_enabled']?'checked':''?>><span>Record recognized crawler requests separately</span></label><label for="analytics-retention">Eligible for cleanup after<select id="analytics-retention" name="retention_days"><?php foreach ([30,90,180,365] as $days): ?><option value="<?=$days?>" <?=(int)$options['retention_days']===$days?'selected':''?>><?=$days?> days</option><?php endforeach; ?></select></label><p class="small muted">Raw IP addresses, full user-agent strings, complete referral URLs, form contents, payment details, and account pages are not stored in analytics. Staff traffic and requests carrying Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control are excluded. Analytics uses the existing first-party session; it does not follow visitors across websites.</p><button class="button" type="submit">Save analytics settings</button></form>
 <details class="analytics-detail"><summary>How these numbers are calculated</summary><dl class="analytics-definitions"><dt>Visits</dt><dd>A browser session starts a new visit after 30 minutes without activity. The same person using another browser or device counts separately.</dd><dt>Bounce rate</dt><dd>Completed visits with exactly one pageview divided by completed visits. Visits active in the last 30 minutes are excluded until they finish. This is a single-page definition, not an engagement-based score.</dd><dt>Active viewing time</dt><dd>The tracker sends small first-party heartbeats while the page is visible and a final update when it becomes hidden. It does not record mouse movements, keystrokes, form fields, or screen recordings.</dd><dt>Live visitors</dt><dd>Visits with activity in the last minute. This panel refreshes about every 15 seconds while open and visible.</dd><dt>Search terms</dt><dd>Only recognized search-engine query parameters supplied in a referral can be recorded. Search Console reports provide broader Google query totals separately, with their own privacy omissions.</dd><dt>Daily totals</dt><dd>A visit spanning midnight may appear on both days. The total for the selected period counts that visit once.</dd></dl></details>
 <details class="analytics-detail"><summary>Clean up expired analytics now</summary><p>Scheduled maintenance also applies this retention setting when enabled in <a href="<?=e(app_url('admin/maintenance/'))?>">Temporary data &amp; retention</a>. Use this bounded cleanup to remove expired analytics records without changing website content or business records.</p><form method="post" class="form-stack"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="prune"><label for="analytics-owner-password">Confirm your owner password<input id="analytics-owner-password" name="owner_password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" required></label><button class="button secondary" type="submit">Remove expired analytics records</button></form></details>
</section>

